 "conclusion": "The model makes sense for lead/solo lines (25% of solo beats shift >= 4 frets, 35% of fast beats) and for the clean part (16%). It does NOT make sense for rhythm guitar: 3.06% overall and 0.23% (2 of 873 beats) on pnd Rhytm Guitar -- the 'machine-gun' rhythm part the guitar profile targets barely moves the fretting hand.",
 "findings_against_task_hypotheses": [
  "Per-beat shift does not keep legato overlap intact. Hammer/pull overlap spans TWO beats (source in beat N, target in N+1); the converter bridges only when origin_tick >= target on_tick, so any target shifted later than its source is left as a gap and re-picked. Existing --humanize already breaks 40-65% of bridgeable pairs (legato_probe). A hand-shift delay is always positive and lands on post-jump beats; on Spring Melody Solo 27 of its 57 shift beats are slide/hammer targets.",
  "Delay as a function of |delta| alone ignores available time: 22% of shift beats follow a rest and 27% have >= 600 ms since the previous fretted attack; on rhythm tracks 30 of 52 shifts have IOI >= 600 ms (section boundaries)."
 ],
